# Integrate Random Forest Model as HHO Objective Function

This plan outlines the integration of the pre-trained `pIC50` Random Forest model (located in `RandomForestRegressor_model/`) as the objective function for the Discrete Harris Hawks Optimization (HHO) algorithm in `hho_script.ipynb`.

## User Review Required

> [!WARNING]
> **Performance Implications**
> The ML model requires 895 features for each SMILES string. Computing the 881 PubChem fingerprints using `padelpy` is an I/O bound process that requires starting a Java application for each molecule. Evaluating a single molecule might take 1-2 seconds.
> A standard HHO run with a population of 20 and 50 iterations could require evaluating over 1,000 unique molecules, which might take **~30 minutes** to complete.

To mitigate the performance impact, a caching dictionary will be implemented so identical molecules are never evaluated twice.

